.SS "template<uint32_t dim> void \fBcsmp::HydroFractureVisitor\fP< dim >::Visit (\fBElement\fP< dim > * n)\fR [virtual]\fP"

.SH "Implementation"
.PP
.IP "1." 4
test whether at least one element node is overpressured\&.
.IP "2." 4
only where an overpressure exists conductivity shall be diffused\&.
.IP "3." 4
back calculating dP/dxy from transport velocity\&.
.IP "4." 4
the conductivity is enhanced propertional to pressure gradient over the storativity, since = dQ / bc\&.
.IP "5." 4
calculating desired flux in element with bc as the proportionality constant between desired pressure change and flux\&.
.IP "6." 4
calculating conductivity needed to accomodate this flux\&. This makes sense only where there is an appreciable pressure gradient\&. Otherwise an increased conductivity will not foster the flow\&. 
.br

.IP "7." 4
only if the new conductivity is greater than the old one it is assigned\&. 
.PP

